<ui version="4.0">
 <class>PrefSortingLayout</class>
 <widget class="QWidget" name="PrefSortingLayout">
  <property name="geometry"><rect><x>0</x><y>0</y><width>520</width><height>300</height></rect></property>
  <property name="windowTitle"><string>Sorting</string></property>
  <layout class="QVBoxLayout" name="topLayout">
   <item>
    <widget class="QGroupBox" name="groupBox_reorder">
     <property name="sizePolicy">
      <sizepolicy hsizetype="Expanding" vsizetype="Fixed">
       <horstretch>0</horstretch>
       <verstretch>0</verstretch>
      </sizepolicy>
     </property>
     <property name="title">
      <string>Reorder Clusters by Similarity (Shift+S)</string>
     </property>
     <layout class="QVBoxLayout" name="reorderGroupLayout">
      <item>
       <layout class="QHBoxLayout" name="reorderMethodRow">
        <item>
         <widget class="QLabel" name="reorderMethodLabel">
          <property name="text">
           <string>Reorder-by-similarity method:</string>
          </property>
         </widget>
        </item>
        <item>
         <widget class="QComboBox" name="reorderMethodComboBox">
          <property name="toolTip">
           <string>Algorithm used by Reorder Clusters by Similarity (Shift+S) to turn the similarity matrix into a cluster ordering. Single-linkage (MST): the maximum-spanning-tree leaf order, very fast (O(N^2)) but tends to chain. Spectral (Fiedler): sort by the Fiedler vector of the similarity Laplacian via a parallel power iteration, often a smoother heatmap gradient. Feature-space (fet centroids): order clusters by the first principal component of their fet-space centroids -- needs no similarity matrix and is O(N) in the cluster count, so it stays fast where Spectral does not at large N. The first two read whichever matrix is computed (error or template). Default: Single-linkage (MST).</string>
          </property>
          <item>
           <property name="text"><string>Single-linkage (MST)</string></property>
          </item>
          <item>
           <property name="text"><string>Spectral (Fiedler)</string></property>
          </item>
          <item>
           <property name="text"><string>Feature-space (fet centroids)</string></property>
          </item>
         </widget>
        </item>
        <item>
         <spacer name="reorderMethodSpacer">
          <property name="orientation"><enum>Qt::Horizontal</enum></property>
          <property name="sizeHint" stdset="0"><size><width>40</width><height>20</height></size></property>
         </spacer>
        </item>
       </layout>
      </item>
      <item>
       <widget class="QCheckBox" name="reorderDisplayOnlyCheckBox">
        <property name="text">
         <string>Reorder matrix display only (do not renumber clusters)</string>
        </property>
        <property name="toolTip">
         <string>When Reorder Clusters by Similarity (Shift+S) runs, rearrange only the rows/columns of the error-matrix display into similarity order, leaving cluster IDs unchanged. This skips the full cluster renumber (rewriting every spike label, rebuilding spikesByCluster, invalidating and recomputing the matrix), so it is near-instant at large cluster counts. The new order is view-only: it is not saved to the .clu file and axis labels will be out of numeric order. Off: renumber clusters into similarity order (persistent, slower). Applies to the error matrix only. Default: off.</string>
        </property>
        <property name="checked"><bool>false</bool></property>
       </widget>
      </item>
     </layout>
    </widget>
   </item>
   <item>
    <widget class="QGroupBox" name="groupBox_mergeRecommend">
     <property name="sizePolicy">
      <sizepolicy hsizetype="Expanding" vsizetype="Fixed">
       <horstretch>0</horstretch>
       <verstretch>0</verstretch>
      </sizepolicy>
     </property>
     <property name="title">
      <string>Recommended Merges (panel under the child palette)</string>
     </property>
     <layout class="QVBoxLayout" name="mergeRecommendGroupLayout">
      <item>
       <layout class="QHBoxLayout" name="mergeRecommendMaxRow">
        <item>
         <widget class="QLabel" name="mergeRecommendMaxLabel">
          <property name="text"><string>Maximum recommendations:</string></property>
         </widget>
        </item>
        <item>
         <widget class="QSpinBox" name="mergeRecommendMaxSpinBox">
          <property name="toolTip"><string>Cap on how many merge recommendations the panel lists, best first. The panel ranks every candidate pair before capping, so raising this lengthens the list rather than widening the search. Default: 20.</string></property>
          <property name="minimum"><number>1</number></property>
          <property name="maximum"><number>200</number></property>
          <property name="value"><number>20</number></property>
         </widget>
        </item>
        <item>
         <spacer name="mergeRecommendMaxSpacer">
          <property name="orientation"><enum>Qt::Horizontal</enum></property>
          <property name="sizeHint" stdset="0"><size><width>40</width><height>20</height></size></property>
         </spacer>
        </item>
       </layout>
      </item>
      <item>
       <layout class="QHBoxLayout" name="mergeRecommendErrorFloorRow">
        <item>
         <widget class="QLabel" name="mergeRecommendErrorFloorLabel">
          <property name="text"><string>Minimum error probability:</string></property>
         </widget>
        </item>
        <item>
         <widget class="QDoubleSpinBox" name="mergeRecommendErrorFloorSpinBox">
          <property name="toolTip"><string>Absolute floor on the symmetrised error-matrix probability. A pair scoring below this is dropped no matter how well the waveform envelopes overlap: the error matrix holds probabilities, so a low value means &quot;these are not one unit&quot; and is a fact, not a ranking. This gate is applied BEFORE ranking, so a disbelieved pair does not occupy a rank slot. Raise it to demand stronger evidence; 0 disables the gate and leaves only the relative quality floor. Default: 0.05.</string></property>
          <property name="decimals"><number>3</number></property>
          <property name="minimum"><double>0.000000000000000</double></property>
          <property name="maximum"><double>1.000000000000000</double></property>
          <property name="singleStep"><double>0.010000000000000</double></property>
          <property name="value"><double>0.050000000000000</double></property>
         </widget>
        </item>
        <item>
         <spacer name="mergeRecommendErrorFloorSpacer">
          <property name="orientation"><enum>Qt::Horizontal</enum></property>
          <property name="sizeHint" stdset="0"><size><width>40</width><height>20</height></size></property>
         </spacer>
        </item>
       </layout>
      </item>
      <item>
       <layout class="QHBoxLayout" name="mergeRecommendQualityFloorRow">
        <item>
         <widget class="QLabel" name="mergeRecommendQualityFloorLabel">
          <property name="text"><string>Minimum combined quality:</string></property>
         </widget>
        </item>
        <item>
         <widget class="QDoubleSpinBox" name="mergeRecommendQualityFloorSpinBox">
          <property name="toolTip"><string>Minimum combined quality for a pair to be listed. Quality is the WEAKER of the two witnesses&apos; percentile ranks, so 0.90 means both the error matrix and the waveform-envelope overlap must rank the pair in their own top decile. Because it is a percentile it is relative to the pairs on offer, which is why the absolute error floor above exists alongside it. Lower it to see more marginal suggestions. Default: 0.90.</string></property>
          <property name="decimals"><number>2</number></property>
          <property name="minimum"><double>0.000000000000000</double></property>
          <property name="maximum"><double>1.000000000000000</double></property>
          <property name="singleStep"><double>0.050000000000000</double></property>
          <property name="value"><double>0.900000000000000</double></property>
         </widget>
        </item>
        <item>
         <spacer name="mergeRecommendQualityFloorSpacer">
          <property name="orientation"><enum>Qt::Horizontal</enum></property>
          <property name="sizeHint" stdset="0"><size><width>40</width><height>20</height></size></property>
         </spacer>
        </item>
       </layout>
      </item>
     </layout>
    </widget>
   </item>
   <item><spacer name="vSpacer"><property name="orientation"><enum>Qt::Vertical</enum></property><property name="sizeHint" stdset="0"><size><width>20</width><height>40</height></size></property></spacer></item>
  </layout>
 </widget>
